From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cpuset: make sure new tasks conform to the current config of the cpuset

A new task copies cpus_allowed and mems_allowed from its parent early in
copy_process() and is linked into its cgroup's task list much later. If
the cpuset rewrites the masks of its tasks in between, the new task is
not on the list yet and keeps the old mask.

With "cpuset: restore the requested CPUs when they come back online" every
hotplug event rewrites those masks, and on this board the hotplug governor
produces such events at each screen-off and screen-on, exactly when
processes and threads are being created. A thread that loses the race
when the screen comes on keeps the screen-off mask (cpu0 only) until the
next hotplug event that changes its cpuset.

Copy the parent's masks again from the cpuset fork callback, which runs
once the task is on the list.

Derived from upstream:
  06f4e9489891 "cpuset: make sure new tasks conform to the current config
               of the cpuset" (v4.8; 87fe0cd807d1 in android-3.18 through
               3.18-stable)

Adapted for 3.10:
- No task_css_is_root(); the root cpuset is recognized by comparing
  task_cs() with top_cpuset under rcu_read_lock().
- cpuset_fork() is static and referenced from cpuset_subsys directly.
  CONFIG_CGROUP_FREEZER already has a fork callback, so
  need_forkexit_callback does not change.

Compile-tested as part of the cpuset series with CONFIG_CPUSETS=y: full
zImage with the GCC 4.9 arm-linux-androideabi prebuilt, and
kernel/cpuset.o and kernel/cgroup.o at every step of the series; no
warnings in the files touched. Not run on the device.

[combined set, 2026-11-06] Header only, the diff is the staged one. The
paragraph above said "five patches". The series was staged as five
(staging/backport-cpusets 0014-0018) and compiled step by step in that
form; the combined set has four of them, 0015-0018. The fifth, "cpuset:
let CAP_SYS_NICE move other users' tasks into a cpuset" (staged 0015),
is replaced by "cgroup: one credential rule for moving another user's
task" (0014). The four were compiled again in that form, as one zImage
build of the whole combined series, not step by step.
---
 kernel/cpuset.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/cpuset.c b/kernel/cpuset.c
index 6e3a067..71a1482 100644
--- a/kernel/cpuset.c
+++ b/kernel/cpuset.c
@@ -2093,6 +2093,25 @@ static void cpuset_css_free(struct cgroup *cont)
 	kfree(cs);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Make sure the new task conforms to the current state of its parent,
+ * which could have been changed by cpuset just after it inherited the
+ * state from the parent and before it sits on the cgroup's task list.
+ */
+static void cpuset_fork(struct task_struct *task)
+{
+	bool in_top;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	in_top = task_cs(task) == &top_cpuset;
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+	if (in_top)
+		return;
+
+	set_cpus_allowed_ptr(task, &current->cpus_allowed);
+	task->mems_allowed = current->mems_allowed;
+}
+
 struct cgroup_subsys cpuset_subsys = {
 	.name = "cpuset",
 	.css_alloc = cpuset_css_alloc,
@@ -2105,6 +2124,7 @@ struct cgroup_subsys cpuset_subsys = {
 	.attach = cpuset_attach,
 	.subsys_id = cpuset_subsys_id,
 	.base_cftypes = files,
+	.fork = cpuset_fork,
 	.early_init = 1,
 };
 
